    "q-71129": {
      "dom_id": "step-q71129",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}=1$ and the line \n$\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2t \\\\ y=2-t, \\\\ z=t-1\\end{aligned}$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$",
      "worked_solution": "Substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the ellipsoid, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2} & =8 \\\\ (2t)^{2}+4(2-t)^{2}+2(t-1)^{2} & =8 \\\\ 4{t}^{2}+4(4-4t+{t}^{2})+2({t}^{2}-2t+1) & =8 \\\\ 4{t}^{2}+16-16t+4{t}^{2}+2{t}^{2}-4t+2 & =8 \\\\ 10{t}^{2}-20t+18 & =8 \\\\ 10{t}^{2}-20t+10 & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}-2t+1 & =0 \\\\ (t-1)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solution $t=1.$\n\nNow, we substitute our solution back into the equations of the line.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=2(1)=2 \\\\ y=2-1=1 \\\\ z=1-1=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(2,1,0).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
