    "q-36325": {
      "dom_id": "step-q36325",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find the projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of one sheet \n$(x+3)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-2{z}^{2}=1$\n and the plane   $x+2z=-3$ onto the\n$xy$-plane.",
      "worked_solution": "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xy$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $z.$ First, we solve the equation of the plane for $z$, as follows:\n\n$$\nx+2z=-3\\,⟹\\,z=-\\frac{x+3}{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $z$ into the equation of the hyperboloid, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-2{(-\\frac{x+3}{2})}^{2} & =1 \\\\ (x+3)^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projection of the intersection is the ellipse $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{2}=1.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
